  "reasons": [
    "Q3's +7% intermodal volume rode a record September for US container imports; retailers now expect cargo volumes to slow into the final months, so that volume does not repeat in Q4.",
    "Consensus for the January print is $0.50 versus $0.39 a year earlier, while the FY level has already been cut 0.68% in 30 days, 3 raises against 5 cuts.",
    "At 24.3x forward earnings and 15.8x EV/EBITDA [enterprise value over earnings before interest, tax, depreciation and amortisation], the price assumes the 39.1% operating margin \u2014 up 880bps \u2014 survives the freight slowdown."
  ],
  "watch": [
    "Intermodal volume: confirms if Q4 growth falls below Q3's +7%; breaks the short if it holds at or above.",
    "Operating margin: confirms if it retreats from 39.1%; breaks if the 880bp gain holds through the quarter.",
    "Revenue against the $4.02B record: confirms if Q4 misses consensus; breaks if the run-rate repeats.",
    "2027 guidance: confirms if management flags softer intermodal; breaks if it raises the volume outlook."
  ],
